AliasNull base userspace - versioned foundation artifact.

This is the first real, versioned AliasNull base-userspace artifact (Part 27-R).
It is NOT a Linux filesystem, a rootfs image, or a set of system tools. It is a
minimal, honest, self-identifying foundation that AliasNull installs into its
private runtime directory and verifies before the runtime reports ready.

It intentionally contains NO executables. No arm64 tool that is genuinely
required for the base runtime can yet be produced reproducibly from this
repository, so none is bundled or faked. Future userland tools (a package
manager, Python, Git, and other optional packages) will be real, separately
produced arm64 components installed on top of this foundation as a later
milestone; this artifact only establishes the versioned base they build upon.

Contents (all files are original AliasNull-authored metadata/documentation):
  VERSION           - the base artifact version (single source of truth)
  ARCH              - the target architecture this build is produced for
  DESCRIPTION       - this description
  PROVENANCE.txt    - provenance and scope of every file in the artifact
  LICENSE.txt       - licensing note for the artifact files

Version:   see VERSION
Arch:      see ARCH
Produced:  deterministically from the AliasNull repository (app/src/main/assets/
           userspace/base) and shipped inside the signed APK.
